From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Silicon Bakery (t6020 port)" <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:42:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slices: the per-frame slice map, from MULTI_SLICE_MAX_MB

V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_MULTI_SLICE_MODE = MAX_MB with MULTI_SLICE_MAX_MB:
slices of whole MB rows (H.264) or 32-line CTB rows (HEVC), as many rows
per slice as MAX_MB holds (one row minimum, at most 32 slices). SINGLE
(the default) writes nothing.

Wire fields:
- [KEXT13.5] AVC_Slice::GenerateMap (0xfffffe0008f556f0) and
  HEVC_Slice::GenerateMap (0xfffffe0008f5c164), reached from
  AVE_Client_GenerateSlicesMap for VideoToolbox's NumberOfSlices: one
  byte per row = slice index, 0x100 rows, in the per-frame slice-header
  block (cmd+0x40): H.264 SH+0x472 (wire 0x4B2) with SH+0x574 (0x5B4)
  zeroed; HEVC S+0x44C (the existing sh_map) with S+0x554 zeroed. Rows
  per slice = (rows left + ceil(slices left / 2)) / slices left, >= 1;
  re-derived here, not copied.
- [FW] CAVCController::PipePrepareParam (0x47ac0) takes the slice count
  as map[rows - 1] + 1, or ceil(MBs / SH+0x574) when that is non-zero.
The coded header's per-slice records were already walked; the slice
cap rises from 16 to 32 ([LIVE] macOS: NumberOfSlices 1..32, 33+
refused). Untested on hardware.
